<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept private machinery orders fall 10.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept private machinery orders fall 10.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's private-sector machinery orders, excluding those for machinery at electric power firms and for ships, fell a seasonally adjusted 10.2 percent in September from the previous month to 946.5 billion yen, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Month-on-month percentage changes, seasonally adjusted, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 SEPT		AUG</p>
<p> Overall		6.5		-19.5</p>
<p> Private	    -10.2		-11.1</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			 SEPT		AUG</p>
<p> Public		16.8		-28.7</p>
<p> External	    28.9		-24.1</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes, not adjusted for seasonal factors, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			 SEPT		AUG</p>
<p> Overall		11.7		-1.8</p>
<p> Private		 3.6		11.4</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			 SEPT		 AUG</p>
<p> Public		 8.9		-11.9</p>
<p> External	    30.3		 -5.3</p>
</text>
